  "id": "log-linear-analysis",
  "term": "log-linear analysis",
  "definition": "Log-linear analysis is a statistical method for studying associations in categorical data. It treats all variables equally rather than designating one as the outcome, which makes it useful for examining interactions, patterns of independence, and higher-order relationships without implying causation.",
